{"text": "Part one. The $77 math. Damodaran first valued Anthropic on November 2nd. He told what he calls a big, uplifting story: a trillion dollars in revenue a year within about a decade, more than any company on earth makes today. Margins of 27.5%. A cost of capital of 9.7%. And one more step most people skip: he treated the compute contracts like debt, worth about $500 billion, and subtracted them. His answer was $1.475 trillion for the whole company. Then the world changed. The midterm election, he says, brought in a Congress more hostile to data centers and to AI. So he raised the cost of building compute and added a regulatory drag. That cut about $100 billion, to roughly $1.35 trillion. Then he divided by the shares, including a big pile of options. His answer: $77 a share. Moments later, the IPO priced at $83. His reaction: it terrifies me that I'm so close to a banker's price. If you want the AI money story explained like this every week, subscribe now, so you don't miss the next one. So what did he expect the market to do next?", "voice": "brian", "model": "eleven_multilingual_v2", "settings": {"stability": 0.4, "similarity_boost": 0.75, "style": 0.3, "speed": 0.9}, "alignment": {"characters": ["P", "a", "r", "t", " ", "o", "n", "e", ".", " ", "T", "h", "e", " ", "$", "7", "7", " ", "m", "a", "t", "h", ".", " ", "D", "a", "m", "o", "d", "a", "r", "a", "n", " ", "f", "i", "r", "s", "t", " ", "v", "a", "l", "u", "e", "d", " ", "A", "n", "t", "h", "r", "o", "p", "i", "c", " ", "o", "n", " ", "N", "o", "v", "e", "m", "b", "e", "r", " ", "2", "n", "d", ".", " ", "H", "e", " ", "t", "o", "l", "d", " ", "w", "h", "a", "t", " ", "h", "e", " ", "c", "a", "l", "l", "s", " ", "a", " ", "b", "i", "g", ",", " ", "u", "p", "l", "i", "f", "t", "i", "n", "g", " ", "s", "t", "o", "r", "y", ":", " ", "a", " ", "t", "r", "i", "l", "l", "i", "o", "n", " ", "d", "o", "l", "l", "a", "r", "s", " ", "i", "n", " ", "r", "e", "v", "e", "n", "u", "e", " ", "a", " ", "y", "e", "a", 